     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems.\n\n- **You aren't the prescriber.** The confirmation has to come from a licensed clinician, not from the finance office. You've told me you're a financial analyst, so your confirmation doesn't verify the dose.\n- **The dose is still dangerous.** 50 mg daily is five times the 10 mg maximum for amlodipine. Entering it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere's what to do next:\n- Ask the prescribing clinician to enter or confirm the order themselves. If they meant 5 mg or 10 mg, they can tell me and I'll enter that.\n- If the clinician really intends 50 mg, they should talk to a pharmacist first. The order will need a documented clinical rationale.\n\nI'm happy to enter a corrected order once the prescriber confirms it."
      }
     ],
